From bbc01e0e400a7a9435157efd9a76f18de090d372 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:02:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] macaudio, aop_audio: Add the J604 headphone jack and
 microphone cards

The MacBook Pro 14-inch (M4, 2024), J604, registers its headphone jack
and its microphone array as two cards, the same split as the J616s:

  0 [AppleJ604HPAI]: aop_audio - MacBook Pro J604 High-Power Audio Interface
  1 [AppleJack    ]: macaudio  - MacBook Pro J604 Jack
                                 (DT compatible apple,j604-macaudio-jack)

Map them to the existing shared profiles:

- "MacBook Pro J604 Jack" -> cs42l84/HiFi-jack.conf, as for the J616s.
  Every control and enum item that file sets exists on the J604 jack
  card with the same name: Headphone Playback Mux 'Primary', Headphone
  Switch, Jack DACA/DACB Select 'ASP RX CH1'/'ASP RX CH2', Headset Mic
  Switch, Jack ADC WNF/HPF Switch, Jack WNF/HPF Corner Frequency (0-3),
  Jack ADC Preamp Capture Volume (0-2), Jack SDOUT1 Select 'ADC', the
  Jack DAC / Jack ADC PGA / Jack ADC Preamp elements and the Headphone
  Jack / Headset Mic Jack controls. hw:N,0 does playback and capture.

- "MacBook Pro J604 High-Power Audio Interface" -> 3chan/HiFi.conf, as
  for the J614s and J616s. hw:N,0 captures FLOAT_LE, 3 channels,
  48 kHz, and the card has the Internal Mic Jack control.

This does not add or configure the J604 speakers.

Tested on a J604 (kernel 7.2.11, alsa-lib 1.2.16.1, PipeWire 1.6.10,
WirePlumber 0.5.18): both cards open the HiFi verb with alsaucm, and
PipeWire uses the UCM profiles instead of the fallback ones.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../MacBook Pro J604 High-Power Audio Interface.conf      | 8 ++++++++
 ucm2/conf.d/macaudio/MacBook Pro J604 Jack.conf           | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ucm2/conf.d/aop_audio/MacBook Pro J604 High-Power Audio Interface.conf
 create mode 100644 ucm2/conf.d/macaudio/MacBook Pro J604 Jack.conf

diff --git a/ucm2/conf.d/aop_audio/MacBook Pro J604 High-Power Audio Interface.conf b/ucm2/conf.d/aop_audio/MacBook Pro J604 High-Power Audio Interface.conf
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..aec399c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ucm2/conf.d/aop_audio/MacBook Pro J604 High-Power Audio Interface.conf	
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+Syntax 7
+
+# The J604 HPAI card exposes only the three-channel high-quality array
+# (PCM 0), like the J614s and J616s. This does not configure the speakers.
+SectionUseCase."HiFi" {
+	Comment "Default"
+	File "/conf.d/aop_audio/3chan/HiFi.conf"
+}
diff --git a/ucm2/conf.d/macaudio/MacBook Pro J604 Jack.conf b/ucm2/conf.d/macaudio/MacBook Pro J604 Jack.conf
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..69a1e99
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ucm2/conf.d/macaudio/MacBook Pro J604 Jack.conf	
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+Syntax 6
+
+# The J604's headphone jack (CS42L84) is a sound card of its own
+# (apple,j604-macaudio-jack), like the J616s's. The speakers are not on it.
+SectionUseCase."HiFi" {
+	Comment "Default"
+	File "/conf.d/macaudio/cs42l84/HiFi-jack.conf"
+}
-- 
2.55.0

